Aim
To write a Python program to evaluate the performance of cricket players based on batting, bowling, and fielding statistics.

Algorithm

Start the program.
Input the number of players n.
Repeat the following steps for each player:
a. Display player number.
b. Input runs scored (rs).
c. Input balls faced (bf).
d. Input number of fours (fours).
e. Input number of sixes (six).
f. Input wickets taken (wk).
g. Input runs conceded (rc).
h. Input overs bowled (ob).
i. Input catches taken (ct).
Calculate:
Batting strike rate → sr = (rs / bf) * 100
Bowling economy → eco = rc / ob
Classify batting performance:
If sr ≥ 150 → Excellent batter
Else if sr ≥ 100 → Good batter
Else → Average batter
Classify bowling performance:
If eco ≤ 6 → Excellent bowler
Else if eco ≤ 8 → Good bowler
Else → Average bowler
Classify fielding performance:
If ct ≥ 3 → Outstanding fielder
Else → Needs improvement
Display results for each player.
Stop the program.

PROGRAM 
n = int(input("Enter no. of players: "))

for i in range(n):
    print("\nPlayer", i+1)

    rs = int(input("Enter the runs scored: "))
    bf = int(input("Enter the balls faced: "))
    fours = int(input("Enter fours: "))
    six = int(input("Enter sixes: "))

    wk = int(input("Enter the wickets taken: "))
    rc = int(input("Enter the runs conceded: "))
    ob = int(input("Enter the overs bowled: "))

    ct = int(input("Enter the catches taken: "))

    # Calculations
    sr = (rs / bf) * 100
    eco = rc / ob

    # Batting performance
    if sr >= 150:
        print("excellent batter")
    elif sr >= 100:
        print("good batter")
    else:
        print("average batter")

    # Bowling performance
    if eco <= 6:
        print("excellent bowler")
    elif eco <= 8:
        print("good bowler")
    else:
        print("average bowler")

    # Fielding performance
    if ct >= 3:
        print("outstanding fielder")
    else:
        print("needs improvement")

